  "id": "Compound::DB00281 - Gene::1555",
  "verbalization": "Lidocaine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Cyp2c18 and Cyp2c8, which are both involved in the epoxygenation of arachidonic acid. This binding likely modulates the enzymatic activity of these cytochrome P450 enzymes, which in turn influences the production of arachidonic acid derivatives. The observed pathway links Lidocaine to Cyp2b6 through a series of enzymatic interactions, suggesting that the inhibition of arachidonic acid metabolism by Lidocaine may indirectly affect Cyp2b6 activity. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible relationship, with the shared involvement of arachidonic acid metabolism as a critical intermediate. The evidence supports a role for Lidocaine in modulating Cyp2b6 function through the regulation of arachidonic acid metabolism, though the exact mechanism of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
